[{:db/id -1, :working/body "# keiei-llm benchmark — gemma-4-E2B-it vs gemma-4-E4B-it\n\n- run: 2026-05-10 ~23:41 → 2026-05-11 ~00:01 UTC (terminated mid-round-3)\n- path: macOS host → kubectl port-forward → keiei-litellm Service → llama-server pod\n- pods: keiei-llm-e2b (request 2c/4Gi · limit 4c/8Gi), keiei-llm-e4b (request 4c/8Gi · limit 6c/12Gi)\n- node: vhf-16c-58gb (Vultr VKE lax)\n- prompts: 5 (hello / short-summary / ja-short / code-explain / structured)\n- captured: 26 requests (21 ok, 5 timeout)\n\n## summary\n\n| model | n_ok | n_err | mean lat (ok) | p50 | p95 | mean tok/s | mean c_tok |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| `gemma-4-E2B-it` | 15 | 0 | 26062 ms | 27226 | 36838 | 10.60 | 276 |\n| `gemma-4-E4B-it` | 6 | 5 | 36501 ms | 41801 | 48617 | 2.48 | 123 |\n\n## by prompt (mean latency / mean tok/s)\n\n| prompt | E2B lat | E2B tok/s | E2B c_tok | E4B lat | E4B tok/s | E4B c_tok | E4B errs |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| hello | 8721ms | 10.56 | 92 | 2634ms | 0.78 | 2 | 0 |\n| short-summary | 24528ms | 10.45 | 256 | 81243ms | 3.72 | 243 | 0 |\n| ja-short | 36873ms | 10.74 | 396 | — | — | — | 0 |\n| code-explain | 33662ms | 10.62 | 357 | 48617ms | 5.08 | 247 | 0 |\n| structured | 26526ms | 10.61 | 281 | — | — | — | 0 |\n\n## findings\n\n- **E2B is faster and stable.** Mean latency ~24s for content-bearing prompts, ~10–11 tok/s, all 15 captured requests succeeded.\n- **E4B is slower and unstable under the LiteLLM 90s `request_timeout`.** Long-context prompts (`ja-short`, `structured`, `code-explain`) repeatedly hit HTTP 408; only short prompts and rare warm-cache replies fit inside the budget.\n- **E4B at full saturation.** `kubectl top pod` showed E4B holding ~5990–5998m CPU (all 6 cores at limit) for minutes per request. Request 5.2 tok/s when not timing out — about half the E2B throughput.\n- **Reasoning trace dominates short prompts.** `hello` returns only 2 completion tokens on E4B and ~89 on E2B, because gemma-4 emits a `reasoning_content` chain-of-thought that consumes the `max_tokens` budget before any visible answer is produced. Bench cap raised from 200 → 400 mid-run.\n- **Implication for the keiei daemon.** With `KEIEI_LLM_TIMEOUT_SEC=20`, E4B will time out on every non-trivial prompt; daemon must pin `KEIEI_LLM_MODEL=gemma-4-E2B-it` until either (a) E4B gets GPU per ADR 2605102100 §6 Phase 4, or (b) the LiteLLM `request_timeout` is raised to 180s AND the daemon timeout raised in lockstep.\n\n## limits of this run\n\n- terminated mid-round-3 (not a full 3×5×2 = 30 sample set)\n- all timing includes the macOS↔VKE port-forward hop (~1–4 ms RTT) and the LiteLLM hop\n- no `--direct` comparison (Cloudflare wildcard Worker `*.gftd.ai` was intercepting before the tunnel; CF Worker route exclusion needed before public/direct path measurements are possible)"}]